.TH QSCHEMA 1 "2026 July 10" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qschema \- database schema management tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qschema
\fBalign\fP|\fBdrop\fP|\fBdiff\fP
\fIconnection\fP
\fIschema-file\fP
[\fIoptions\fP]
.PP
.B qschema
\fBexport\fP
\fIconnection\fP
[\fIoptions\fP]
.PP
.B qschema
\fBvalidate\fP|\fBinfo\fP
\fIschema-file\fP
[\fIoptions\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqschema\fR manages database schemas from YAML (\fB.ysm\fP) or JSON
(\fB.jsm\fP) schema definition files.
It can align a database to match a schema, show differences, validate
schema files, and export existing database schemas.
The legacy \fBschema\-reverse\fP command is a compatibility alias for
\fBqschema export\fP.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Database and Schema-File Commands"
.TP
.B align
Align the database to match the schema definition.
.TP
.B drop
Drop all objects defined in the schema from the database.
.TP
.B diff
Show differences between the database and the schema.
.SS "Database Export Command"
.TP
.B export
Export the current database schema; requires a connection but no input schema
file.
.SS "File-Only Commands (require schema-file only)"
.TP
.B validate
Validate a schema file for correctness.
.TP
.B info
Display information about the schema file.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Schema Management Options"
.TP
.B \-\-data\-ts =\fIname\fP
Data tablespace name.
.TP
.B \-\-index\-ts =\fIname\fP
Index tablespace name.
.TP
.B \-\-access\-level =\fIlevel\fP
Access level: \fBuntrusted\fP, \fBtrusted\fP (default), or \fBadmin\fP.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force the operation without confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show the SQL that would be executed without running it.
.SS "General Options"
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable color output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SS "Export Options"
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-schema =\fIname\fP
Set the schema name in the output (default: \fBExportedSchema\fP).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIfile\fP
Write the data-schema document to \fIfile\fP instead of standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-format =\fIformat\fP
Export format: \fByaml\fP (default) or \fBjson\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-with\-partitions
Include physical table partitions in exported schema files.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-table [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching tables.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-seq [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching sequences.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-type [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching types.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mview [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching materialized views.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-proc [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching procedures.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-func [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching functions.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-pkg [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching packages.
.PP
Each export \fIpattern\fP can be an exact name, a comma-separated list, or a
regular expression.
A selection option without a value selects all objects of that type.
Selections can be combined; without any selections, the whole schema is
exported.
.PP
Plain views cannot be exported because the data-schema format has no
representation for them.
.SH EXAMPLES
Align a database with a schema:
.RS
.B qschema align mydb schema.ysm
.RE
.PP
Show differences:
.RS
.B qschema diff mydb schema.ysm
.RE
.PP
Dry-run alignment:
.RS
.B qschema align mydb schema.ysm \-n
.RE
.PP
Export a database schema:
.RS
.B qschema export mydb \-o exported.ysm
.RE
.PP
Export a database schema including physical partitions:
.RS
.B qschema export mydb \-o exported.ysm \-\-with\-partitions
.RE
.PP
Export selected tables as JSON:
.RS
.B qschema export mydb \-\-table='workflows,.*step.*' \-\-format json
.RE
.PP
Validate a schema file:
.RS
.B qschema validate schema.ysm
.RE
